Description: Ship no AppArmor profile, like Mozilla's own package.
 The packaging installs /etc/apparmor.d/usr.bin.firefox, an enforcing profile named firefox written for Ubuntu
 14.10. Its preinst disables it only on a fresh install and on an upgrade from a version before 3.7, so an upgrade
 from Mozilla's package, whose version is higher, enables it. It then replaces the profile of the same name which
 Ubuntu's apparmor package ships in /etc/apparmor.d/firefox, which allows everything and grants the user namespaces
 Firefox's sandbox needs. Under the old profile Firefox cannot lock its profile directory, create its Wayland
 proxy socket or run bwrap for glycin's image loaders, and GTK aborts when it fails to load an icon.
 .
 This drops the profile and everything the maintainer scripts do for it: disabling it in preinst, creating its
 local and abstraction include files and loading it in postinst, and removing those files in postrm, so the
 package does not touch /etc/apparmor.d at all. It does not remove the profile from a system where an earlier
 build installed it. README.Debian describes the profile and is replaced accordingly.
Author: Mitar
Forwarded: https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/firefox/+bug/2172775
Last-Update: 2026-11-02
